From 820a1db2b6209083d144e942f085f9fe559dc371 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: allcodernet <67543055+allcodernet@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 23:56:50 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 28/45] decide: sequential fields (after)

Fields are scored level by level (spec 5): one branch phase per
"after" level in every round. A dependent field's branches start with
its answer lines (its ancestors' stem text, answer value and ",\n",
in declaration order) and use its context trie, cached per request by
(field, lines) and checked at the tail join; full-path plans are
rebuilt on the context trie. The budget reserves the worst-case lines;
more cells after a phase is a 500. Answers of dependent fields carry
"given", the engine block "phases", dump entries "phase" (and "lines"
and "given" for dependent fields). LLAMA_DECIDE_FAULT=rc1-phase1 fails
the first phase-1 decode of each round's first attempt. The "after"
guard is removed.

New decide-after.h/.cpp holds the model-free parts (phases, lines,
worst-case line tokens, context-trie cache, join check);
test-decide-after runs them in ctest with the Qwen2 and Gemma 4 vocab
files.
